window.docContents[104].resolve({"/5___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Further-results/5___17___-The-hook-length-formula/Section-5___17___-The-hook-length-formula/#Chapter5___Introduction_5___17":{"contents":"\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t5. Representations of finite groups: Further results\t5.17. The hook length formula\tSection 5.17: The hook length formula","header":"Section 5.17: The hook length formula","id":"/5___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Further-results/5___17___-The-hook-length-formula/Section-5___17___-The-hook-length-formula/#Chapter5___Introduction_5___17"},"/5___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Further-results/5___27___-Representations-of-semidirect-products/Semidirect-product-definition-and-construction-of-V_____LPAR_O___U_RPAR____/#Chapter5___Discussion_semidirect_products":{"contents":"Let G, A be groups and let \\phi : G \\to \\operatorname{Aut}(A) be a homomorphism. For a \\in A, denote \\phi(g)a by g(a). The semidirect product G \\ltimes A is defined to be the product A \\times G with multiplication law\n\n(a_1, g_1)(a_2, g_2) = (a_1 g_1(a_2), g_1 g_2).\n\nClearly, G and A are subgroups of G \\ltimes A in a natural way.\n\nWe would like to study irreducible complex representations of G \\ltimes A. For simplicity, let us do it when A is abelian.\n\nIn this case, irreducible representations of A are 1-dimensional and form the character group A^\\vee, which carries an action of G. Let O be an orbit of this action, x \\in O a chosen element, and G_x the\nstabilizer of x in G. Let U be an irreducible representation of G_x. Then we define a representation V_{(O,U)} of G \\ltimes A as follows.\n\nAs a representation of G, we set\n\n\nV_{(O,x,U)} = \\operatorname{Ind}_{G_x}^G U = \\{f : G \\to U | f(hg) = hf(g), h \\in G_x\\}.\n\n\nNext, we introduce an additional action of A on this space by (af)(g) = x(g(a))f(g). Then it is easy to check that these two actions combine into an action of G \\ltimes A. Also, it is clear that this representation does not really depend on the choice of x, in the following sense. Let x, y \\in O and g \\in G be such that gx = y, and let g(U) be the representation of G_y obtained from the representation U of G_x by the action of g. Then V_{(O,x,U)} is (naturally) isomorphic to V_{(O,y,g(U))}. Thus we will denote V_{(O,x,U)} by V_{(O,U)} (remembering, however, that x has been fixed).\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t5. Representations of finite groups: Further results\t5.27. Representations of semidirect products\tSemidirect product definition and construction of V_{(O,U)}","header":"Semidirect product definition and construction of V_{(O,U)}","id":"/5___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Further-results/5___27___-Representations-of-semidirect-products/Semidirect-product-definition-and-construction-of-V_____LPAR_O___U_RPAR____/#Chapter5___Discussion_semidirect_products"},"/9___-Structure-of-finite-dimensional-algebras/9___3___-The-Cartan-matrix-of-a-finite-dimensional-algebra/#chapter-09___section-9-3":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t9. Structure of finite dimensional algebras","header":"9.3. The Cartan matrix of a finite dimensional algebra","id":"/9___-Structure-of-finite-dimensional-algebras/9___3___-The-Cartan-matrix-of-a-finite-dimensional-algebra/#chapter-09___section-9-3"},"/9___-Structure-of-finite-dimensional-algebras/9___6___-Finite-abelian-categories/Section-9___6___-Finite-abelian-categories/#Chapter9___Introduction_9___6___heading-1":{"contents":"Let \\mathcal{C} be a k-linear abelian category in which any object has finite length (i.e., a finite filtration whose successive quotients are simple). Assume that for every simple object X of \\mathcal{C}, one has \\operatorname{End}(X) = k. Note that in such a category, Hom spaces are finite dimensional (check it!).\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t9. Structure of finite dimensional algebras\t9.6. Finite abelian categories\tSection 9.6: Finite abelian categories","header":"9.6. Finite abelian categories","id":"/9___-Structure-of-finite-dimensional-algebras/9___6___-Finite-abelian-categories/Section-9___6___-Finite-abelian-categories/#Chapter9___Introduction_9___6___heading-1"}});
